// error
// SPEC §10.7, #3838: §10.5's field default is a CLASS-field production. A
// trait field carries no default -- `trait_field = [ "export" ] IDENT ":"
// type .` is unchanged -- so `=` here stays the parse error it has always
// been, before this ticket and after it. This is a grammar decision, not an
// oversight: a trait field is injected into every using class (§10.7), so a
// default on one raises an override question (#3370) that this ticket does
// not answer, and answering it by accident is worse than not answering it.
//
// Pinned as a parse cascade rather than one clean diagnostic because that IS
// what an unexpected token in a member list produces here -- the parser
// retries the member as each admissible shape. The load-bearing line is the
// first one: `=` is not accepted after a trait field's type.
trait Holds {
  x: int = 5
}

fn main() {
  print("no\n")
}
